====================================================================================================================================
Stage 5 — Tool calling
          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
        This is where the chatbot becomes an agent-like enterprise assistant.
        
        Imagine a banking chatbot.
        
            User: What is my account balance?
        
        The LLM shouldn't invent the balance.
        
          Instead:
                    User
                     │
                     ▼
                    LLM
                     │
                     │ "I need account balance"
                     ▼
                    Tool Selection
                     │
                     ▼
                    getAccountBalance()
                     │
                     ▼
                    Banking API
                     │
                     ▼
                    ₹82,450
                     │
                     ▼
                    LLM
                     │
                     ▼
                    User
So we introduce a generic tool abstraction:

                      public interface ChatTool {
                      
                          String name();
                      
                          ToolResult execute(ToolRequest request);
                      }

Then applications register tools:
                Banking Application
                       │
                       ├── getAccountBalance
                       ├── getTransactions
                       ├── blockCard
                       └── downloadStatement


              Insurance:
                    Insurance Application
                           │
                           ├── getPolicy
                           ├── getClaimStatus
                           ├── createClaim
                           └── getPremium

The chatbot platform doesn't need to know what these tools actually do.

That's the key abstraction.
