One very important design principle

Don't start with microservices.

Start with a modular monolith.

For example:

chatbot-platform
│
├── api
│
├── conversation
│
├── orchestration
│
├── llm
│
├── rag
│
├── tools
│
├── security
│
├── configuration
│
└── observability

Initially:

                ONE APPLICATION
                     │
        ┌────────────┼────────────┐
        │            │            │
   Conversation     RAG         Tools

Once we identify actual scaling boundaries:

Once we identify actual scaling boundaries:

Chat Service
Conversation Service
RAG Service
Tool Service
LLM Gateway
Config Service

become separate services.

This is much better architecture than starting with 15 microservices simply because we're building an "AI platform."


